WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.240
Okay, so an agent harness is the runtime layer around the model,

2
00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:08.233
and you need one because an API call is stateless.

3
00:00:08.233 --> 00:00:12.653
A research agent might make thirty to fifty calls in one task,

4
00:00:12.653 --> 00:00:16.553
so the harness runs the loop while the model only reasons.

5
00:00:16.633 --> 00:00:18.513
The hard part is checkpointing,

6
00:00:18.513 --> 00:00:23.793
because without it a run that fails at step eighteen restarts from the beginning.

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:28.960
So I'd save state after each step and make the tools idempotent,

8
00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:32.500
which means a repeated call gives the same result.

9
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:37.360
Then a failed run resumes from its last checkpoint instead of starting over.
